    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "\nSuperbly located 5 bed terraced home with elevated views\n\nSavills is delighted to present 30 Sunday's Well Road to the market, a superb five-bedroom terraced residence occupying one of Cork's most sought-after addresses. Elevated above the city, this impressive period home enjoys views of some of Cork's most recognisable landmarks and offers a rare opportunity to acquire a property of exceptional character, scale and potential in a location renowned for its convenience and enduring appeal.\n\nEntering from road level, the front door opens to a spacious entrance porch, with steps leading down to the principal accommodation. The home immediately impresses with its generous proportions and remarkable outlook. The two elegant front reception rooms are among its standout features, overlooking the mature gardens towards Fitzgerald's Park, University College Cork, the Mardyke and the western side of the city. Rich in original detail, the property retains ornate fireplaces, decorative ceiling coving and picture rails, providing a wonderful foundation for restoration and modernisation. This floor also accommodates a fifth bedroom, family bathroom and gated external access via an outside staircase. \n\nThe lower ground floor comprises a kitchen and dining room on one side, with two substantial storage rooms on the other. Offering excellent scope for reconfiguration, this level could readily accommodate a more contemporary layout with expanded living and family spaces. Direct access leads to the rear patio, while a separate service yard includes a WC and two useful storage sheds, ideal for everyday family requirements. Upstairs, the first floor hosts four spacious double bedrooms. The two front-facing rooms continue to benefit from the property's outstanding elevated views, while the generous proportions throughout reflect the character and quality associated with these historic Sunday's Well homes.\n\nOutside, the south-facing rear gardens are a truly exceptional feature. Arranged over two tiers, the upper level provides a private lawn ideal for entertaining, relaxation and family use. The lower tier offers further potential and, subject to the necessary consents, could accommodate additional landscaping, garden rooms, workshops, hobby spaces or ancillary accommodation. It is a rare opportunity to enjoy such extensive outdoor space within easy reach of Cork city centre.\n\nThe location of 30 Sunday's Well Road is sure to appeal to a broad range of purchasers. Situated just moments from the heart of Cork City, the property offers the convenience of being able to walk into the city centre in approximately 20 minutes, while UCC, Cork University Hospital and MTU are all within easy reach. The immediate neighbourhood is home to an excellent range of local amenities including cafés, pubs, shops, gyms, sports clubs and recreational facilities, while nearby parks and scenic walks reflect the rich history and character that make this part of Cork so highly regarded.\n\nAlthough requiring complete renovation, this remarkable property offers an outstanding opportunity for buyers seeking to create a bespoke family home in a prestigious city location. First-time buyers, those trading up and purchasers with a passion for restoration will immediately recognise the potential on offer, while astute investors may also appreciate the long-term value presented by such a significant property in a prime setting. \n\nEarly viewing is highly recommended to fully appreciate the scale, character and potential of this unique home. Arrange your private viewing with Savills today."
      },
      {
